    <div id="p-0137" num="0141" class="description-paragraph">Referring to Table 2, the separators according to the examples included the acrylic copolymer including a specific structural unit and thus exhibited excellent adhesive strength to a substrate, moisture characteristics, and heat resistance.</div>
    <div id="p-0138" num="0142" class="description-paragraph">While this invention has been described in connection with what is presently considered to be practical embodiments, it is to be understood that the invention is not limited to the disclosed embodiments, but, on the contrary, is intended to cover various modifications and equivalent arrangements included within the spirit and scope of the appended claims.</div>
    
  </div>
  </div>
  </section>

  <section itemprop="claims" itemscope>
    <h2>Claims (<span itemprop="count">13</span>)</h2>
    
    <div itemprop="content" html><div mxw-id="PCLM483458183" lang="EN" load-source="patent-office" class="claims">
    <claim-statement>The invention claimed is:</claim-statement>
    <div class="claim"> <div id="CLM-00001" num="00001" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">1. A separator for a lithium secondary battery, comprising
<div class="claim-text">a porous substrate, and</div>
<div class="claim-text">a coating layer on at least one surface of the porous substrate,</div>
<div class="claim-text">wherein the coating layer comprises</div>
<div class="claim-text">an acrylic copolymer;</div>
<div class="claim-text">an organic filler; and</div>
<div class="claim-text">inorganic particles,</div>
<div class="claim-text">wherein the acrylic copolymer comprises a first structural unit derived from (meth)acrylamide, and a second structural unit derived from (meth)acrylic acid or (meth)acrylate, and a third structural unit derived from (meth)acrylamidosulfonic acid or a salt thereof represented by one selected from Chemical Formula 4, Chemical Formula 5, Chemical Formula 6, and a combination thereof,</div>
</div>
      <div class="claim-text">
        <chemistry id="CHEM-US-00005" num="00005">
          <div class="patent-image"><a href="https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/95/3b/2f/d83aa77d2e9f89/US12230834-20250218-C00005.png"><img id="EMI-C00005" he="150.11mm" wi="59.69mm" file="US12230834-20250218-C00005.TIF" alt="Figure US12230834-20250218-C00005" img-content="chem" img-format="tif" orientation="portrait" inline="no" width="239" height="600" alt="Figure US12230834-20250218-C00005" class="patent-full-image" src="https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/95/3b/2f/d83aa77d2e9f89/US12230834-20250218-C00005.png"/></a></div>
          <attachments>
            <attachment idref="CHEM-US-00005" attachment-type="cdx" file="US12230834-20250218-C00005.CDX"> </attachment>
            <attachment idref="CHEM-US-00005" attachment-type="mol" file="US12230834-20250218-C00005.MOL"> </attachment>
          </attachments>
        </chemistry>
        <div class="claim-text">wherein, in Chemical Formula 4 to Chemical Formula 6,</div>
        <div class="claim-text">R<sup>4 </sup>to R<sup>6 </sup>are each independently hydrogen or a C1 to C6 alkyl group,</div>
        <div class="claim-text">L<sup>1 </sup>to L<sup>3 </sup>are each independently a substituted or unsubstituted C3 to C10 alkylene group, a substituted or unsubstituted C3 to C20 cycloalkylene group, a substituted or unsubstituted C6 to C20 arylene group, or a substituted or unsubstituted C3 to C20 heterocyclic group,</div>
        <div class="claim-text">a, b, and c are each independently one of integers of 1 or 2, and</div>
        <div class="claim-text">M is an alkali metal,</div>
        <div class="claim-text">wherein the organic filler is included in an amount of 0.1 to 50 wt % based on a total amount of the organic filler and the inorganic particles, and</div>
        <div class="claim-text">wherein the first structural unit is included in an amount of 55 mol % to 95 mol % based on 100 mol % of the acrylic copolymer, and the total amount of the second structural unit and the third structural unit is included in an amount of 5 mol % to 45 mol % based on 100 mol % of the acrylic copolymer.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00002" num="00002" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">2. The separator of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, wherein the coating layer has a thickness of 1 μm to 5 μm.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00003" num="00003" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">3. The separator of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, wherein the average particle diameter of the organic filler is 0.1 μm to 0.5 μm.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00004" num="00004" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">4. The separator of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, wherein the organic filler is at least one organic compound selected from an acrylate-based compound and a derivative thereof, a diallyl phthalate-based compound and a derivative thereof, a polyimide-based compound and a derivative thereof, a copolymer thereof, and a mixture thereof.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00005" num="00005" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">5. The separator of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, wherein the average particle diameter of the inorganic particles is 0.3 μm to 0.7 μm.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00006" num="00006" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">6. The separator of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, wherein the inorganic particles comprise Al<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>, SiO<sub>2</sub>, TiO<sub>2</sub>, SnO<sub>2</sub>, CeO<sub>2</sub>, MgO, NiO, CaO, GaO, ZnO, ZrO<sub>2</sub>, Y<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>, SrTiO<sub>3</sub>, BaTiO<sub>3</sub>, Mg(OH)<sub>2</sub>, boehmite, or a combination thereof.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00007" num="00007" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">7. The separator of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, wherein the second structural unit derived from the (meth)acrylic acid or (meth)acrylate is included in an amount of 0 mol % to 40 mol % based on 100 mol % of the acrylic copolymer, and the third structural unit derived from the (meth)acrylamidosulfonic acid or the salt thereof is included in an amount of 0 mol % to 10 mol % based on 100 mol % of the acrylic copolymer.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00008" num="00008" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">8. The separator of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, wherein
<div class="claim-text">the first structural unit derived from (meth)acrylamide is represented by Chemical Formula 1, and</div>
<div class="claim-text">the second structural unit derived from the (meth)acrylic acid or (meth)acrylate is represented by one of Chemical Formula 2, Chemical Formula 3, and a combination thereof:</div>
</div>
      <div class="claim-text">
        <chemistry id="CHEM-US-00006" num="00006">
          <div class="patent-image"><a href="https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/d1/d9/7c/28bd8313f0b27c/US12230834-20250218-C00006.png"><img id="EMI-C00006" he="96.18mm" wi="58.59mm" file="US12230834-20250218-C00006.TIF" alt="Figure US12230834-20250218-C00006" img-content="chem" img-format="tif" orientation="portrait" inline="no" width="234" height="385" alt="Figure US12230834-20250218-C00006" class="patent-full-image" src="https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/d1/d9/7c/28bd8313f0b27c/US12230834-20250218-C00006.png"/></a></div>
          <attachments>
            <attachment idref="CHEM-US-00006" attachment-type="cdx" file="US12230834-20250218-C00006.CDX"> </attachment>
            <attachment idref="CHEM-US-00006" attachment-type="mol" file="US12230834-20250218-C00006.MOL"> </attachment>
          </attachments>
        </chemistry>
        <div class="claim-text">wherein, in Chemical Formula 1 to Chemical Formula 3,</div>
        <div class="claim-text">R<sup>1 </sup>to R<sup>3 </sup>are each independently hydrogen or a C1 to C6 alkyl group,</div>
        <div class="claim-text">R<sup>7 </sup>is a substituted or unsubstituted C1 to C20 alkyl group.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00009" num="00009" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">9. The separator of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, wherein a weight average molecular weight of the acrylic copolymer is 350,000 to 970,000.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00010" num="00010" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">10. The separator of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, wherein a volume ratio of the inorganic particle and the organic filler is 40:1 to 1:3.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00011" num="00011" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">11. The separator of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, wherein a weight ratio of the acrylic copolymer:organic filler and inorganic particle is 1:20 to 1:40.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00012" num="00012" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">12. A lithium secondary battery, comprising
<div class="claim-text">a positive electrode, a negative electrode, and the separator of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref> between the positive electrode and the negative electrode.</div>
</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim"> <div id="CLM-00013" num="00013" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">13. A separator for a lithium secondary battery, comprising
<div class="claim-text">a porous substrate, and</div>
<div class="claim-text">a coating layer on at least one surface of the porous substrate,</div>
<div class="claim-text">wherein the coating layer comprises</div>
<div class="claim-text">an acrylic copolymer;</div>
<div class="claim-text">an organic filler; and</div>
<div class="claim-text">inorganic particles,</div>
<div class="claim-text">wherein the acrylic copolymer comprises a first structural unit derived from (meth)acrylamide, and a second structural unit derived from (meth)acrylic acid or (meth)acrylate, and a third structural unit derived from (meth)acrylamidosulfonic acid or a salt thereof represented by one selected from Chemical Formula 4, Chemical Formula 5, Chemical Formula 6, and a combination thereof,</div>
</div>
      <div class="claim-text">
        <chemistry id="CHEM-US-00007" num="00007">
          <div class="patent-image"><a href="https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/8c/e1/24/a6fab73ab9efdb/US12230834-20250218-C00007.png"><img id="EMI-C00007" he="150.11mm" wi="59.69mm" file="US12230834-20250218-C00007.TIF" alt="Figure US12230834-20250218-C00007" img-content="chem" img-format="tif" orientation="portrait" inline="no" width="239" height="600" alt="Figure US12230834-20250218-C00007" class="patent-full-image" src="https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/8c/e1/24/a6fab73ab9efdb/US12230834-20250218-C00007.png"/></a></div>
          <attachments>
            <attachment idref="CHEM-US-00007" attachment-type="cdx" file="US12230834-20250218-C00007.CDX"> </attachment>
            <attachment idref="CHEM-US-00007" attachment-type="mol" file="US12230834-20250218-C00007.MOL"> </attachment>
          </attachments>
        </chemistry>
        <div class="claim-text">wherein, in Chemical Formula 4 to Chemical Formula 6,</div>
        <div class="claim-text">R<sup>4 </sup>to R<sup>6 </sup>are each independently hydrogen or a C1 to C6 alkyl group,</div>
        <div class="claim-text">L<sup>1 </sup>to L<sup>3 </sup>are each independently a substituted or unsubstituted C3 to C10 alkylene group, a substituted or unsubstituted C3 to C20 cycloalkylene group, a substituted or unsubstituted C6 to C20 arylene group, or a substituted or unsubstituted C3 to C20 heterocyclic group,</div>
        <div class="claim-text">a, b, and c are each independently one of integers of 1 or 2, and</div>
        <div class="claim-text">M is an alkali metal,</div>
        <div class="claim-text">wherein the organic filler is included in an amount of 0.1 to 50 wt % based on a total amount of the organic filler and the inorganic particles, and</div>
        <div class="claim-text">wherein the first structural unit derived from the (meth)acrylamide is included in an amount of 80 mol % to 85 mol % based on 100 mol % of the acrylic copolymer, the second structural unit derived from the (meth)acrylic acid or (meth)acrylate is included in an amount of 10 mol % to 15 mol % based on 100 mol % of the acrylic copolymer, and the third structural unit derived from the (meth)acrylamidosulfonic acid or the salt thereof is included in an amount of 5 mol % to 10 mol % based on 100 mol % of the acrylic copolymer.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div> </div>
  </div>
  </section>

